# Captured evidence — byte-exact, never line-ending-normalized.
#
# Every digest in SHA256SUMS is over the bytes the Jetson produced. A checkout
# that rewrote CRLF/LF (autocrlf on Windows, say) would change those bytes and
# `sha256sum -c` would fail on a bundle nobody had tampered with — turning the
# self-verification claim into a false alarm. `-text` switches EOL conversion
# off so the files survive any checkout unchanged.
ENVIRONMENT.txt -text
GIT_COMMIT      -text
SHA256SUMS      -text
integrity.txt   -text
trials.jsonl    -text
